    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d501">

                <pb facs="0639" n="554" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg554"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">612.119/2748</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Mexican Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bonillas</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-01-07"><hi rendition="#italic">January 7,
                        1920</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. F–493</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have had the honor to send to Your
                    Excellency the following notes<anchor n="37" xml:id="d501-f1"/> on the dates
                    herewith below stated: <table cols="2" rows="11">
                        <row role="label">
                            <cell>A 4375</cell>
                            <cell>July 7, 1919</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>A 4619</cell>
                            <cell>August 29, 1919</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>F 80</cell>
                            <cell>September 13, 1919</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>F 240</cell>
                            <cell>October 21, 1919</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>F 255</cell>
                            <cell>October 27, 1919</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>F 301</cell>
                            <cell>October 31, 1919</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>F 305</cell>
                            <cell>November 3, 1919</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>F 318</cell>
                            <cell>November 8, 1919</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>F 326</cell>
                            <cell>November 11, 1919</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>F 364</cell>
                            <cell>November 17, 1919</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell>F 373</cell>
                            <cell>November 22, 1919</cell>
                        </row>
                    </table>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#flush">in which I applied to Your Excellency for your good offices in
                    obtaining licenses for the export of war material.</p>
                <p>No answer having been received as yet to the above mentioned notes, I
                    respectfully beg Your Excellency kindly to let me know <pb facs="0640" n="555"
                        xml:id="pg555"/> whether they have been received and what decision you may
                    have been pleased to render thereon.</p>
                <p>Thanking you most earnestly in advance for the attention you may be pleased to
                    give to the matter, I beg [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Y. Bonillas</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
